THESE INSTRUCTIONS ARE PRIMARILY INTENDED FOR LINUX PLATFORMS

To create simulation input files use program init.py or edit input files manually.

In initialization program init.py you can edit object list, object orbital parameters, and simulation configuration settings.
Edit the file in your preferred text editor.

To run the initialization program init.py open folder in console and type: python3 init.py

config.txt parameters in order (it is recommended to create the file through init.py):
1. Number of objects; 2. Index of units (1=m|s|kg, 2=au|day|kg, 3=pc|year|M_sol); 3. Index of center object (0=center of mass); 
4. Simulation duration in chosen units; 5. Number of simulation steps; 
6. Step interval of console outputs; 7. Step interval of position file saves

To run simulation open folder in console and type: ./simulation
    NOTE! If the expected output file size exceeds one gigabyte, the program will ask for permission to proceed.

To plot the simulation run plot.py by opening the folder in console and typing: python3 plot.py
    NOTE! To get object names correct in the plot do initialization through init.py or edit target_sequence.txt manually.